<article class="env-lemma" id="0BV8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BV8">Lemma <span data-tag="0BV8">48.21.7</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0F42" data-tag="0F42">48.16.1</a> let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of $\textit{FTS}_ S$. If $f$ is Cohen-Macaulay (More on Morphisms, Definition <a href="/tag/045R" data-tag="045R">37.22.1</a>), then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  f^!\mathcal{O}_ Y = \omega _{X/Y}[d]  \]
</div>
  <p> for some coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module $\omega _{X/Y}$ flat over $Y$ where $d$ is the locally constant function on $X$ which gives the relative dimension of $X$ over $Y$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The relative dimension $d$ is well defined and locally constant by Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02NM" data-tag="02NM">29.30.4</a>. The cohomology sheaves of $f^!\mathcal{O}_ Y$ are coherent by Lemma <a href="/tag/0AU1" data-tag="0AU1">48.17.6</a>. We will get flatness of $\omega _{X/Y}$ from Lemma <a href="/tag/0BV6" data-tag="0BV6">48.21.4</a> if we can show the other cohomology sheaves of $f^!\mathcal{O}_ Y$ are zero. 
    <p>
      The question is local on $X$, hence we may assume $X$ and $Y$ are affine and the morphism has relative dimension $d$. If $d = 0$, then the result follows directly from Lemma <a href="/tag/0BV7" data-tag="0BV7">48.21.6</a>. If $d > 0$, then we may assume there is a factorization 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  X \xrightarrow {g} \mathbf{A}^ d_ Y \xrightarrow {p} Y  \]
</div>
    <p>
       with $g$ quasi-finite and flat, see More on Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/0BUU" data-tag="0BUU">37.22.8</a>. Then $f^! = g^! \circ p^!$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0AA1" data-tag="0AA1">48.17.3</a> we see that $p^!\mathcal{O}_ Y \cong \mathcal{O}_{\mathbf{A}^ d_ Y}[-d]$. We conclude by the case $d = 0$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>